WEBVTT

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.190
Hold it right there!

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:35.320
I remember you!

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.200
Let's do it! Three!

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.160
Two!

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.240
--One!

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.290
--Go, Shoot!

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.160
What's going on?

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.590
What we saw that day in the park

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:55.590
was an intense battle between Dunga's
Voltic Ape and Yuya's copied Sacred Beast.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.010
Blow him away!

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.790
Digital Bird!

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:41.180
The copied Sacred Beast was powerful!

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.310
No one expected
it to be this strong!

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.820
I lost... I totally lost...!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.660
Damn!

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:08.250
Damn! Damn! Damn!

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.160
Goddammit!!

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.710
I'm just holding you guys back.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.340
I should just quit the team...!

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.550
Want one?

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.840
These are pretty good, you know.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.050
Mariam...

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:26.850
Just win next time.
So cheer up already.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.520
Mariam...

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.560
Mariam...!!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.480
You don't have to cry, it's okay.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.360
You are so simple.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.570
I've never met someone so
easily led on by a woman.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.700
I didn't expect the digital
Sacred Beasts to be so powerful.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.000
It might be do or die time then.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:13.020
Why did it release all
that power back then?

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:18.230
Just what the hell happened?

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.820
What's this program?

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:40.000
No! Impossible!

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.510
The digital Sacred Beast is evolving.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:49.430
Yes. Somehow, a self-evolution program has been installed into the digital Sacred Beast.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:55.230
A system that learns in the midst of
battle and automatically improves itself!

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.190
And that's why...

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.990
It's a miracle! A scientific miracle!

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:07.370
This is exactly what we need to make your
dreams of capturing the Sacred Beasts a reality!

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:12.120
We must continue to let it gain experience and make our Sacred Beasts evolve!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.920
Which means that obtaining the four
Sacred Beasts is no mere pipe dream.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:17.120
Yes, sir!

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.000
However, there is one problem.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.130
A problem?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.510
The Bladers, sir.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:28.050
That Yuya boy couldn't withstand the evolved power of Digital Bird.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:33.930
In order to master the continuously evolving
digital Sacred Beast one needs to be Blader with

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:38.900
physical endurance and
an incredible force of will.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.380
Run wild! Bite right into him! Digital Bird!

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:08.300
You're the strongest Sacred Beast in the world! No, of all time!

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.310
I can't fight.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:15.310
Yuya!

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:17.600
Yuya!

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.570
If I was a little more careful...

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.610
Yuya, I will get revenge for you.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.240
Three! Two! One!

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.330
Go, Shoot!

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.510
The air drag is unbalanced!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.300
Concentrate a little more, please!

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.090
Crap!

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.510
Don't let up!

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.450
What the hell are you doing?

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.240
You weren't even trying!

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.000
Takao, what happened?

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.080
The last run was so much better!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:21.920
How am I supposed to know?

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.750
Be serious for once!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.210
I am, aren't I?

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:28.210
You aren't! You need more concentration!

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:31.800
Do you think you can beat the
copied Sacred Beasts like that?

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:32.970
What?!

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:37.390
According to my calculations, Seiryu
doesn't even come close to beating one!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.810
That's crossing the line!

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.230
Just stop, you two!

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.310
You've all been on
edge all morning!

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.440
I know that copied Sacred Beast
from yesterday was something else...

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.690
But so what?

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:51.740
It's natural to panic a little, right?

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:54.070
What's that supposed
to mean, Hiromi?

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:58.120
Are you saying we're scared of them?

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.040
That's not what I meant...

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.210
They're just copies, right?

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.540
I would never lose to a copy!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:08.920
I'm just saying practicing
like this is totally pointless!

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.510
What was that?

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.630
Takao, that's too far!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:15.050
But it's true!

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:18.180
If you guys wanna do it,
then do it yourselves!

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:23.140
I don't think you'll win, though.
Not in a million years.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:24.480
Now you've done it!

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.560
Stop it!

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:30.990
Why do you guys have to get like this
over some dumb copied Sacred Beasts?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.150
Isn't this the most
important time?

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:36.530
Isn't this when the BBA
team should act as one?

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:40.240
You can't win if you
fight among yourselves!

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.870
What good is a team?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.540
The team is only as
strong as the weakest link.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.500
We won't win any battles
acting like a pity party.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.630
Takao, are you serious?

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:56.720
Fine. Do what you want.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.970
Don't come crying to me!

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:01.600
Kyoujyu!

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:02.680
Takao!

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.730
If he wants to leave, he can leave!

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.770
I'll fight my own way!

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:11.900
Nothing good will come from
being on a team with these guys.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.070
I can't take it anymore.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.410
I'm over this.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.040
I guess this is the end of the BBA team.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:23.620
Max! Rei!

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:24.830
Takao...!

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.790
Takao! Are you okay with this?

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.920
I can't let this happen.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:00.160
A cookout?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.330
The weather's so nice out!

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:06.000
Let's all have some fun for once!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.420
I've got Beyblade practice to do.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.670
Even though someone like me
would be wasting his time.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:17.090
You can't just practice all day.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:19.470
Sometimes you need a change of pace.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:21.510
So let's get to it!

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.060
We don't have to go right?

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.390
'Cause I ain't going.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.980
I said you're going so
get your butt in gear!

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:28.980
Okay!

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.700
Kyoujyu will handle the meat.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.950
Rei and Max will handle the veggies.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:42.620
Please and thank you!

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.200
Guess we have to.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:46.750
Let's get started, then.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.290
Takao, you better help too!

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:56.170
Screw your cookout.
I'm staying out of this stupid crap!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.920
Gosh...

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:12.230
"International Airport"

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.230
Japan, huh?

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.690
It's good to be back.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:17.740
Yeah.

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.950
Go! Yeah!

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.210
Go, Shoot!

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.090
Nice one, Kane!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.720
Here's your Bey, kid. Glad it's safe.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:40.930
Thanks!

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.600
You two should't play here. It's dangerous.

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:47.100
Make sure you
play in a stadium.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.640
Yeah! We will, miss!

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:51.730
We won't play here anymore.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:55.310
Let's get moving.

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:56.650
See ya.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:57.980
Be careful out there.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:15.960
"Bakuten Shoot Beyblade 2002"

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.970
Eat as much as you like!

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:24.430
This is the perfect
day for a cookout!

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:25.550
That's it!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.300
The sauce is delicious!

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.140
Did you make this yourself?

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:33.060
Yup! It's got ginger, garlic
and apple cider mixed in!

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.520
It's so good!

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.060
It tastes better outside!

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:38.440
It sure does.

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:42.740
Just one more left.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.910
Meat's all done.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:49.200
I cooked the best
parts just for you.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:49.910
Okay!

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.040
I can't hold back anymore!

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.910
You jerks!

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:05.510
I'll never forgive you
if you eat my plate!

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.310
I was going to eat that!

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.940
Don't sweat the details!

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:16.650
That was mine!

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.400
And now it's mine!

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.230
That's mine too!

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:21.480
Sucks for you!

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.610
You eat too fast!

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:25.570
Hey, that's mine!

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:28.990
Way too fast!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.700
Now, now...

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:31.450
Mhm!

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.370
Man I'm full...

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.580
I can't move!

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.300
It feels so good.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.970
I don't remember the last
time we just kicked back.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:52.890
We've been straining ourselves
with all the battling.

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.440
That thing sure was strong.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.030
For a copy, even.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:07.320
Really strong.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:10.120
Can we beat it?

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.910
What are you backing down for?
You just gotta do it!

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.540
You're right.
We just gotta do it.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.120
We just have to...

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.590
This one's big!

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.310
Takao!

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:39.390
Grandpa!

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:40.600
Over there!

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:41.730
Let's check it out.

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.270
Help me!

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.360
I can't swim!

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:47.900
Grandpa!

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:48.990
Takao!

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:50.200
Grandpa!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:53.620
Hold on, Grandpa!
I'll save you!

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.410
Wait!

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:56.410
Stop!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:01.420
What if you get caught
up in the river, too?!

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.540
What?

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:05.210
He'll be fine,
just leave it to us!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.380
Right there!

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:11.390
Calm down, sir!

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:14.470
We'll save you,
so hang in here!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:19.350
The flow of the river...
the depth... and the width...

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:23.520
If I calculate it with
the size of that tree...

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.820
What are they going to do?

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.450
Goki! Ten meters
at twelve o'clock!

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.320
Okay!

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.880
Wow! A perfect calculation!

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:51.630
I think he's fine.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:54.220
You can't take
your eyes off him.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.720
You guys are amazing.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.350
Your teamwork was on point.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:15:59.980
Well, yeah.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.230
We're a team.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:02.140
A team?

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:08.230
So you're all Bladers?

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:17.620
You train by traveling
all over the world?

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:20.950
It's not just to get stronger, though.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:22.920
What do you mean?

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:26.000
It's important to improve of course,

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:30.210
but by traveling the world we see
and experience all sorts of things.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:34.930
I don't think there's a point to
battling without being aware of all that.

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:35.720
I agree.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.470
Hm?

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:40.890
It's because a Beyblade is like
an extension of the Blader.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:41.930
Yes.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.650
Is that really true?

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.060
Damn right it is!

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.780
A battle isn't just about the
Beys clashing against each other.

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:54.030
It's about two Bladers throwing
everything they've got at each other.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.280
Well then, I agree.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:58.910
You want to go a round?

00:16:59.160 --> 00:16:59.990
Sure.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.140
This is going to be
an interesting battle.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.640
Takao! You can do it!

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:20.600
Here we go!

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:23.480
Three! Two! One!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.640
--Go, Shoot!

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.900
I'm gonna show
you all I've got!

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.400
Go!

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:35.110
Dragoon!

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:38.320
I won't lose!

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.870
He can match Takao
blow-for-blow. He's good!

00:17:46.870 --> 00:17:49.330
It's been ages since
I've seen a battle like this!

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:53.420
I can feel your spirit!

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.930
Go!

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.730
He's pretty good.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:11.360
His speed and judgment
with his Bey are good.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.030
He's no average Blader.

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:19.530
I'm gonna finish this quick!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.000
Keep it up Takao! That's the way!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.580
He's struggling to
dodge all your attacks!

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:33.630
No, he's judging Dragoon's speed!

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.430
I can hardly believe it.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:45.520
He's perfectly matching Dragoon's speed!

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.020
He's slowing down.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.690
It's almost time.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.740
I don't think he'll survive
it at that spin speed.

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:01.740
Here it comes!

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:04.990
Dragoon!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:12.290
He took it!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:15.800
How could he
withstand it at that speed?

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:18.010
Go!

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.930
He's got Dragoon on the defense!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.720
Takao! You can do it!

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:30.480
This guy's amazing.
I'm sure that was his special move.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:33.900
It failed, and yet he's just
as confident as before!

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:35.690
He should be shocked.

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:38.110
But it didn't
faze him at all.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:41.320
He's got incredible spirit.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:46.450
Darn it!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.450
Now it's over!

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.830
I won't lose!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.800
It's a draw.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.100
Not bad!

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.350
Likewise.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:11.940
I haven't had such a good
feeling battle in so long.

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:15.020
I'm Takao Kinomiya.
Nice to meetcha.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:18.400
Kane Yamashita.
Nice to meet you.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:20.940
See you later!

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:22.950
Later!

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.120
Let's go another round someday!

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.330
Alright. Let's clean up and go home.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:33.080
Yeah.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.920
Kane Yamashita...

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:38.130
I'll remember that name.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.800
Mr. Gideon, they have arrived.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:46.220
Come in.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.390
Come on!

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:52.770
Good to see you again, Mr. Gideon.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.650
We've been waiting for you.
Our strongest Bladers...

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:59.190
Kane Yamashita.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:00.320
Goki.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.110
Jim. And Salima.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:04.910
How were your travels?

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:08.120
Good. We learned a lot.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.910
Good to hear.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:15.580
There's only one reason I called
you back from your travels.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:16.420
Doctor?

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.210
Yes!

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:21.550
What are these?

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:27.010
These are the ultimate Beyblades, which we have poured all of our development resources into.

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:28.640
Take them.

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:29.890
Take them...

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:34.180
And you will become
the ultimate Bladers.

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:03.400
Kane and his friends were a
part of Team Psykick all along.

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:08.320
We infiltrate their base in order
to see the truth for ourselves.

00:23:09.070 --> 00:23:11.490
I've always wanted to try this.

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:15.370
Like, "Kyoujyu, this is your mission, should you choose to accept it!"

00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:18.080
Chairman! Don't ignore me!

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:20.420
Don't miss the next episode, alright?
